Nightforge: keeps controller input from Windows games while Nightforge's overlay is up.

The overlay asks through a Darwin notification with a time limit (pad_silence.h): until Nightforge asks
this does nothing, and if Nightforge hangs or crashes the silence ends by itself. Only winebus.so
changes: nothing is loaded into a game and no game file is touched; the game sees a pad at rest.

diff --git a/dlls/winebus.sys/bus_sdl.c b/dlls/winebus.sys/bus_sdl.c
index 2ce5fa9..68a64c2 100644
--- a/dlls/winebus.sys/bus_sdl.c
+++ b/dlls/winebus.sys/bus_sdl.c
@@ -32,6 +32,7 @@
 #include <unistd.h>
 #include <sys/types.h>
 #include <dlfcn.h>
